  "live_records": {
    "q-37957": {
      "dom_id": "step-q37957",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Evaluate the repeated integral ${\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{e}^{2x}\\,}{y}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x}{y}]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{y}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{y}{[\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}]}_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{y}(\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{0}}{2})\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{{e}^{2}-1}{2y}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{{e}^{2}-1}{2y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\frac{{e}^{2}-1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{y} \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{e}^{2}-1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}-1}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2({e}^{2}-1)}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
