      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "${\\int }_{3}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{4}({5}^{y-3}\\sqrt{x})\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{4}[{\\int }_{0}^{4}({5}^{y-3}\\sqrt{x})\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{3}^{4}{5}^{y-3}[{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{4}{5}^{y-3}{[\\frac{2}{3}{(\\sqrt{x})}^{3}]}_{0}^{4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{4}{5}^{y-3}(\\frac{2}{3}{(\\sqrt{4})}^{3}-\\frac{2}{3}{(\\sqrt{0})}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{4}\\frac{16\\cdot {5}^{y-3}}{3}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{4}\\frac{16\\cdot {5}^{y-3}}{3}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\frac{16}{3}{[\\frac{{5}^{y-3}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}]}_{3}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}(\\frac{{5}^{4-3}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}-\\frac{{5}^{3-3}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}(\\frac{5-1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{64}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
