    "q-72047": {
      "dom_id": "step-q72047",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "${\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x[{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,[\\operatorname{sin}⁡y]_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-0)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\sqrt{2}[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x]_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}(0-(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\sqrt{2}}^{2}}{2} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
